    "0B hotspot flag: by mean_top3, mutated rpoB sits at mean percentile 98.5 in resistant genomes vs 96.4 for WT rpoB (among proteins \u2265 30 aa) \u2014 i.e. it is pushed into the high tail an attention pool could attend to. hotspot_z recomputed with a MAD floor of 0.732 to remove the MAD\u21920 blow-ups in the raw statistic.",
    "SNP distance profile (masked, n=100): mean surprisal is 8.14 at the SNP, 0.11 at \u00b11, 0.19 at \u00b12, 0.16 at \u00b15, vs gene-wide background 0.50 \u2014 the signal is a sharp single-residue spike.",
    "Neighbour test: the SNP is the top-1 masked anomaly in 72% of isolates; the 2nd/3rd most-surprising residues lie within \u00b12 aa of the SNP in 9%/3% of isolates (median distance 617/8 aa) \u2014 so 'use top-3' is NOT justified by a neighbour smear."
